$t=4$ (first lane closure), $t=21$ (second closure), $t=22$ (the accident,
the deepest pass) and $t=21$ (the conflict pass).  In the route panels the
grey line is the plan before the repair and the coloured line is the plan
after it; the robots whose route does not move are exactly the robots that
the pass classifies as \code{delayed\_only} or unchanged.}
\label{fig:cards}
\end{figure}

\subsubsection*{The five phases of a pass}

The phases of a repair are not a slideshow of the grid changing --- the
schedule does not change \emph{within} a pass.  They are the stages of
\code{repair\_schedule} drawn on the freeze tick of the pass, which is what
makes them a useful diagnostic: the banner names the phase and the rung that
ended up resolving the pass, while the plan underneath is the single plan
that the pass is working on.

